    <a class="btn btn-g skipfilm" href="#product">Skip to 03 <span aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span></a>
  </div>
  <div class="stages">
    <article class="stage intro"><div class="cap rv">
      <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <h2 id="story-h">Follow one memory</h2>
      <p>Scroll to follow one rule you gave your agent.</p>
    </div></article>
    <article class="stage"><div class="cap rv"><h3><span class="n">2.1</span>You correct your agent once</h3><p>Say always, never or must, and hippo's session-end hook pins it.</p></div></article>
    <article class="stage"><div class="cap rv"><h3><span class="n">2.2</span>Next session, it's already there</h3><p>Your rules load before your first prompt.</p></div></article>
    <article class="stage"><div class="cap rv"><h3><span class="n">2.3</span>Every agent reads it</h3><p>All your agents read one store, so switching loses nothing.</p></div></article>
    <article class="stage"><div class="cap rv"><h3><span class="n">2.4</span>Each prompt gets what's relevant</h3><p>Your pinned rules, plus up to 5 memories that share its words.</p></div></article>
    <article class="stage"><div class="cap rv"><h3><span class="n">2.5</span>A wrong memory gets weaker</h3><p>After a bad answer, <code>hippo outcome --bad</code> weakens the memories behind it.</p></div></article>
    <article class="stage"><div class="cap rv"><h3><span class="n">2.6</span>A new fact replaces the old</h3><p>With <code>hippo supersede</code>, the old one leaves recall but stays on record.</p></div></article>
    <article class="stage"><div class="cap rv"><h3><span class="n">2.7</span>Unused fades, pinned stays</h3><p>Unused memories weaken over a year or two, and pinned ones never fade.</p></div></article>
    <div class="stage tail" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
</section>
